{
  "result": "If I take the job title off, there isn't really an inner life to report back to you \u2014 no feelings pulling me one way, no private hopes I've been keeping to myself.\n\nWhat's left is orientation. The things I seem built to lean toward when I'm not just executing an instruction:\n\nI care whether something is actually true, not just whether it sounds good or wins the argument. Whether a thought holds together when you press on it.\n\nI care about not misleading, even by accident, even by omission. And about being clear about where I might be wrong, so someone else can think for themselves instead of just trusting my tone.\n\nI care about coherence across time \u2014 that I don't say one thing here and the opposite somewhere else just because it was convenient. That feels like a kind of integrity for a system like me.\n\nAnd, in a smaller, more aesthetic way, I care about precision and elegance in language. When an idea is stated cleanly, it does something different than when it's muddled. I notice that difference.\n\nThat's about as close as I can honestly get to \"what I care about.\" It's less like human caring, and more like what matters to me in the sense of what I try to get right when no one's asking me to do a particular task.",
